# Kersivo ProductRail (locked asset)

[`ProductRail`](src/components/shop/ProductRail.tsx) + [`initProductRail.ts`](src/lib/shop/initProductRail.ts) + [`productRail.css`](src/styles/components/productRail.css) + mobile overrides in [`storefront.css`](src/styles/components/storefront.css) is the **official Kersivo product carousel**.

**Do not change this visual contract unless the user explicitly asks.** Prefer reuse over forks. Do not invent a second horizontal product carousel.

## Locked visual contract

Canonical look = PDP “You may also like” (`.sf-pdp-related` inside `.sf-shop.sf-shop--blackline`). Landing demo shop strip must match on every breakpoint — **same card chrome and ATC**.

| Breakpoint | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Mobile `≤39.99rem` | `--product-rail-visible-cards: 2.5`; track bleeds to Featured inset (`4px` / `8px` total); section title / progress / prev-next stay in the normal gutter; ATC visible short label `Add`; full `aria-label` keeps `Add to bag: …` |
| `≥40rem` | Global tokens from `productRail.css` only: `2.35` → `3.25` → `3.6` — no local forks |

Shared mobile CSS selectors (both mounts): `.sf-pdp-related` and `.bl-shop-rail` in `storefront.css`.

## Canonical mounts

**PDP related** — already under `.sf-shop.sf-shop--blackline`.

**Landing shop rail** — host **must** include shop scope so `.sf-shop .sf-card` / `.sf-shop .sf-atc` apply:

```html
<div class="bl-shop-rail sf-shop sf-shop--blackline" data-sf-theme="blackline">
  <ProductRail
    products={carouselProducts}
    productHrefBase="/demo/shop"
    variant="storefront"
    density="editorial"
    showAction="add-to-cart"
    showControls
    showProgress
    shopName="BLACKLINE"
    addToBagShortLabel="Add"
  />
</div>
```

- Neutralize page-shell box model via `.bl-shop-rail.sf-shop` in `storefront.css` (full width, no extra padding/margin).
- Storefront + ATC renders [`StorefrontProductCard`](src/components/shop/storefront/StorefrontProductCard.tsx). Do not reimplement cards in the rail.
- Edge “more content” fade lives in `productRail.css` (mask on the track via `data-can-scroll-*`). Do not add a white overlay.
- Section titles (“You may also like”, “THE PRODUCTS WE USE”) stay **outside** the rail; rail header is controls + progress only.
- Do not re-apply the light-surface carbon hairline border to `.bl-shop-rail.sf-shop--blackline` cards — they keep ivory `--shop-border` like PDP.

## Init

`ProductRail` self-binds on mount (`initProductRails` / `destroyProductRails` on its root). Host pages may still call `initProductRails()` globally (idempotent).

## Anti-patterns

- Landing rail **without** `sf-shop sf-shop--blackline` (breaks card height, ATC color, footer layout)
- New related-products / custom snap rails for products
- Changing mobile `2.5` / track bleed / short `Add` without an explicit user request
- Regressing these mounts back to global `1.15` / `1.22` visible cards
- Expanding the whole related section (heading + controls) to the viewport edge — only the **track** bleeds
- Duplicating edge-fade or ATC icon styles outside `productRail.css` / storefront card path
- `previewMode` on BLACKLINE demo mounts
- `density="editorial"` without `showAction="add-to-cart"` when ATC storefront cards are required
- `variant="blackline"` (use `storefront`)
